{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceH2","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceClassNotUnique"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mixMarkov_not_isMarkov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mixMarkov_not_isMarkov","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L316-L324","doc":"**(M3) has teeth.** The signed Ocneanu mixture `t_Z` of\n`QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceClassNotUnique` satisfies every field of the `MarkovTrace` class\nbut is **not** a Markov trace in the sense of (M3): if it were, `markovTraceH4A_unique`\nwould force it to equal `markovTraceH4A K q Z`, which it does not (they differ by `6` on\n`σ₀σ₁σ₂`). Over any field with `6 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.markovTraceH4A_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.markovTraceH4A_unique","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L309-L314","doc":"**Uniqueness on `H₄(q)` — the first application of `markov_trace_unique`.** Every\n`MarkovTrace` on the tree's `H₄(q)` satisfying (M3) is the Ocneanu trace\n`markovTraceH4A` at its own Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.isMarkov_H4A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.isMarkov_H4A","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L261-L307","doc":"**The `H₄(q)` trace satisfies (M3)**, for every `z`.\n\n* `i = 0`: the lower subalgebra is `K · 1`.\n* `i = 1`: it lies in `iota34` of the `H₃` span of `{1, σ₀}`; the trace of `x·σ₁` is\n  carried to `H₃` by `iota34_mulσ₁` and `trM4_iota34_stabilizes`, and peeled by\n  `H3.trM_markov_σ₁`.\n* `i = 2`: it lies in `iota34 (H₃)`, and `trM4_markov_σ₂` is exactly the peel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s1_mem_iotaSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s1_mem_iotaSub","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L253-L259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s0_mem_iotaSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s0_mem_iotaSub","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L245-L251","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.one_mem_iotaSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.one_mem_iotaSub","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L241-L243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.low3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.low3","kind":"def","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L230-L239","doc":"The `H₃` coordinates of the span of `{1, σ₀}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iotaSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iotaSub","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L217-L228","doc":"`H₃(q)` inside `H₄(q)`: the elements whose coordinates are `iota34` of an `H₃`\nvector, cut down further by a predicate on that vector closed under the linear\noperations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_unit","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L214-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_zero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L211-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_smul","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L208-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.iota34_add","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L205-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.markovTraceH3A_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.markovTraceH3A_unique","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L189-L193","doc":"**Uniqueness on `H₃(q)`.** Every `MarkovTrace` on the tree's `H₃(q)` satisfying (M3)\nis `markovTraceH3A` at its own Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.isMarkov_H3A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.isMarkov_H3A","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L170-L187","doc":"**The `H₃(q)` trace satisfies (M3)**, for every `z`. At `i = 1` the lower subalgebra\nis `lowH3`, where `H3.trM_markov_σ₁` is exactly the peel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mem_lowH3_of_mem_adjoin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mem_lowH3_of_mem_adjoin","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L156-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lowH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lowH3","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L144-L154","doc":"The subalgebra generated by `σ₀` lies in the span of `{1, σ₀}`: the coordinates on\n`σ₁, σ₁σ₀, σ₀σ₁, σ₀σ₁σ₀` vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s1_v","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s1_v","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L141-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s0_v","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mul_s0_v","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L138-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.markovTraceH2_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.markovTraceH2_unique","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L122-L126","doc":"**Uniqueness on `H₂(q)`.** Every `MarkovTrace` satisfying (M3) is `markovTraceH2` at its\nown Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.isMarkov_H2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.isMarkov_H2","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L107-L120","doc":"**The `H₂(q)` trace satisfies (M3)**, for every `z`. There is one generator, so the\nonly condition is at `i = 0`, on `R · 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mem_span_one_of_mem_adjoin_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mem_span_one_of_mem_adjoin_empty","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L91-L97","doc":"The level-`0` case at every `n`: the subalgebra generated by no generators is\n`R · 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mem_of_mem_adjoin_of_mul_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceIsMarkov.mem_of_mem_adjoin_of_mul_mem","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceIsMarkov.lean#L72-L89","doc":"**A submodule containing `1` and closed under right multiplication by `S` contains\nthe subalgebra generated by `S`.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}